# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and the Makefile picks it up automatically:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env          # fill in DATABASE_URL
#   make migrate-up
#
# The Makefile sources this file with the shell, so values keep quotes and
# characters like `#`. Exporting the variables instead also works, and the file
# wins when both are set. The Go binary itself reads the *process environment*
# (plus an optional YAML file named by CONFIG_FILE) — it is `make` that loads
# this file, not the app.
#
# ENCODING: the DSN is a URL, so characters special to URLs must be
# percent-encoded inside the password. This is not a `make` quirk — it is how
# the DSN parser works:
#     #  ->  %23      @  ->  %40      :  ->  %3A      /  ->  %2F
#     ?  ->  %3F      %  ->  %25     space -> %20
# A raw `#` is read as the start of a fragment, which makes the host unparseable
# (`invalid port ":p" after host`). `make check-db` reports this immediately.
# Simplest alternative: pick a dev password with no special characters at all.
#
# The dev PostgreSQL lives in the VirtualBox VM (see AGENTS.md). Its address is
# DHCP-assigned, so no address is written down here — look it up.
#
# DATABASE_URL is left commented out on purpose: an empty assignment here would
# override a value you had exported for this shell.
#
# Required. There is no default anywhere in the codebase: `make` fails with a
# message naming this variable when it is unset (see internal/config/config.go).
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://<user>:<password>@<vm-address>:5432/<database>?sslmode=disable

# HTTP server
PORT=8080
SERVER_HOST=0.0.0.0

# development | production
APP_ENV=development
APP_NAME=cuanku-api
APP_VERSION=0.1.0

# debug | info | warn | error
LOGGER_LEVEL=info

# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API. The SvelteKit app
# proxies through its own /api/** routes, so this only matters for other callers.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# Optional YAML config file; env vars above always win over it.
# CONFIG_FILE=config.yaml
